"max":0.25},"unit":"cup","dim":"volume","scale":"linear","scaleNote":null,"gramsPerCup":null,"size":null,"optional":false,"aisle":"produce","pantry":false,"shop":true,"one":"fresh parsley"}],"steps":[{"text":"Bring the water and pasta salt to a boil and cook the linguine until just al dente. Save {qty 1 cup fixed} of the pasta water, then drain.","uses":[0,1,2]},{"text":"Meanwhile pat the shrimp dry and season with the salt. Heat the oil and 1 tbsp butter in the skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the shrimp in one layer until pink on the bottom, {time 1 min}, then turn and cook for {time 1 min} more. Move to a plate; they’ll finish in the sauce.","uses":[3,4,5,6]},{"text":"Lower the heat to medium, add the garlic and pepper flakes and stir until the garlic is pale golden, {time 1 min}.","uses":[7,8]},{"text":"Add the wine and lemon juice and simmer until reduced by half, {time 2 min}. Swirl in the remaining butter.","uses":[9,10]},{"text":"Add the pasta, shrimp and a splash of pasta water and toss until the sauce is glossy and the shrimp are opaque, {time 1 min}. Toss in the parsley and serve.","uses":[11]}]}